---
status: Success
--- stdout
Print the canonical form, the geometry, and other properties of a signature in orbifold notation

Usage: escher info [OPTIONS] <SIGNATURE>

Arguments:
  <SIGNATURE>  The signature in orbifold notation, such as *632. In a POSIX shell, put a signature that contains *, (, or ) in single quotes, as in '2*(12)'

Options:
      --check            Verify the fundamental domain of the signature and print the result of each check
      --presentation     Print the generators and relators of the signature and of its fundamental domain, and for a spherical signature the group order by coset enumeration
      --colourings       Print the valid colourings of the fundamental domain, in which no two neighbouring tiles share a colour, one for each conjugacy class of subgroups, with its id, up to the largest number of colours
      --max-colours <N>  The largest number of colours of the valid colourings to count and list, and with --wythoff the largest number of pictures of the arrangements to list, counted over all kinds of polygon, from 1 to 64 [default: 12]
      --wythoff <MARKS>  List the arrangements of the polygons of a Wythoff construction, as three digits as for render, such as 010 for the heptagons of *732 or 111 for its 14-gons, hexagons, and squares. Each arrangement puts one of its pictures, A, B, and so on, on every polygon, and with several kinds of polygon each picture name starts with the position of the corner of its kind, such as 1B. The number of its id is twice the number of sides of a polygon times the number of pictures for one kind of polygon, and a multiple of the least index for several kinds. For each edge of each picture, it lists the edge of the neighbour that lies on it and whether that neighbour is turned or mirrored, with the edges numbered counterclockwise around each mask from edge 0, the edge with the black tick, and with several pictures each edge written after the name of its picture, such as B2 or 1B2
  -h, --help             Print help
